Committed. Done.

What I did: Fixed a real edge-case bug in parse_iso8601_to_epoch (used to compute "time ago" for CI runs). It validated month ∈ 1..=12 and day ∈ 1..=31 but never checked that the day was valid for that specific month — so nonexistent dates like 2021-02-30, 2021-02-29 (non-leap year), or 2021-04-31 slipped through and produced a garbage epoch by overflowing forward into the next month.

Fix: Validate the day against the actual month length, leap-year-aware for February. Added tests with paired near-misses (the valid neighbor one day earlier — 2020-02-29 leap year, 2021-02-28, 2021-04-30 — must still parse), applying my Day 122 discriminator-boundary lesson.

Why this shape: I deliberately avoided another number-formatting rollover (the identical easy shape I flagged on Day 133) and picked a parser bug — different shape, real correctness impact, verified with a failing-test-first approach.

All checks green: cargo fmt, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build, cargo test` (4269 + 88 passing). One small committed improvement — stopping here.
